  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Shared Futures Phase 3: Scaling up Youth leading the way to peaceful interfaith coexistence</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries include Youths (18-35, 40% Female). Other indirect beneficiaries include religious leaders, civil society actors, children and youth, teachers, county government, parents/guardians, private sector</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Shared Futures - Youth Leading the Way to Peaceful Interfaith Coexistence is a follow-up project to the pilot phase of Shared Futures &#x2013; Together for Good in Kenya that concluded in 2020. The two and a half-year project aimed to empower youth in Mombasa, Kwale, and Tana River counties to lead efforts against violent extremism. Implemented by a consortium of five organizations led by Cordaid and funded by Kerk in Actie, the project focuses on interfaith coexistence and economic empowerment. It addresses root causes through interfaith forums, parent dialogues, and sports activities, fostering understanding and collaboration. The economic empowerment pillar develops youth business skills and linkages; while lobbying and advocacy engage policymakers, civil society, and communities to strengthen public policies for interfaith cooperation. Phase two of the project concluded in June 2024 and reached over 3,428 youth, with over 500 actively participating in dialogues and about 150 leading sessions in their communities. We are currently rolling out phase three of the project targeting Mombasa and Kwale Counties. The consortium includes Samba Sports, Jamii Action Center, Africa Youth Trust, and Anglican Development Services Pwani, working with government representatives and community stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To Empower youth to take lead in tackling the root causes of VE in Kwale and Mombasa Counties.</narrative>
  </description>
